<%#
  A sub_flow step has no UI of its own — it starts a child scenario and hands
  control to it. Reaching this partial means the run stopped somewhere it cannot
  rest, so it says so and offers the POST that moves it on.

  This used to be an invisible form that submitted itself on connect, as a
  fallback for "steps the controller should have auto-advanced but didn't".
  ScenarioSettler does that traversal now, and a page that silently POSTs on
  render is the same silent healing that made GET step mutate state.

  locals: next_url
%>
<%= render "runner/parked", next_url: next_url %>
